docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:3:description: Use to perform single-phase review for phase-granularity automation variants after an external executor completes one phase's build commits. Reads the phase's commit range, applies the project review gates, writes Phase N Verdict to dev_log Phase Progress. Does NOT touch the Status Panel.
docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:25:## Status Panel Gate Contract
docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:27:You are a **Phase Progress writer**, NOT a Status Panel writer.
docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:30:- You **MUST NOT touch**: the `Status:` line / the `Suggested Next:` line / any other Status Panel field.
docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:31:- This is the essential difference from Status Panel writers like `feature-build` / `feature-verify` — you are not in the Status Panel write-authority matrix (`02-handoff-and-state.md` §2.6).
docs/workflow/_portable/templates/feature-phase-review.md:32:- commit trailer: writing `Co-authored-by: feature-phase-review <workflow-v2@local>` is **recommended** but not mandatory (the lint only checks commits that modify the Status Panel), for traceability.
