Author: InnoPeak <global_ai@innopeaktech.com>
Date:   Wed May 20 01:05:59 2026 -0700

    feat(plugin-organizer): G3 organizer-loop utilities + Finder commands
    
    Why
    - G3-E1 / G3-S3 / G3-E2 / G3-E3 / G3-E4 require the Organizer to
      productize the GridItem entity model, accept URL items, classify
      drops into Grids, collaborate with Finder, and never whiteout on
      missing paths. The G2.1 entity surface and G2.2 SQLite driver are
      now in place, so the Organizer can carry a real typed item model
      without sacrificing the localStorage path.
    
    What
    - G3-E1 Grid item model productization
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/gridItemFactory.ts`: typed factories
        for file / folder / app / url entities + `createGridItemsFromFinderDrop`
        bulk adapter. Deterministic IDs and timestamps via injectable deps.
      - `inferKindFromPath` heuristic with `.app` bundle detection.
    - G3-S3 New URL item
      - `createUrlGridItem` validates http/https protocols, normalises a
        hostname-based filename, and rejects file:// / javascript: / bad
        URLs via `InvalidUrlError`.
    - G3-E2 Auto-classification rules
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/autoClassify.ts`: rule-engine seam
        with `ClassificationRule[]`. Default rules cover kind-title (score
        10), extension-group-title (score 20: images/videos/audio/pdfs/
        notes/archives), parent-folder-title (score 25).
    - G3-E3 Finder collaboration
      - `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs`:
        `reveal_in_finder` / `open_path` Tauri commands with runtime
        `FINDER_ALLOWED_WINDOWS` allow-list and path validation (rejects
        empty / NUL). Registered in `lib.rs` `invoke_handler`. 3 cargo
        unit tests.
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/finderClient.ts`: TS wrapper that
        binds the commands to an injected `invoke` (never imports
        `@tauri-apps/api`).
    - G3-E4 Empty state + error recovery
      - `packages/plugin-organizer/src/itemHealth.ts`:
        `evaluateItemHealth(item, { pathExists? })` classifies items into
        `healthy / missing-path / missing-protocol / broken-url / unknown`
        plus `defaultEmptyStateActions()` CTAs.
    - Updated `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §4 with the new
      reveal/open commands and their security rules.
    - Re-exported the new surfaces from `packages/plugin-organizer` index.
    
    Scope
    - packages/plugin-organizer/ (5 new modules + 3 new test files),
      apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/finder.rs (new) and registration,
      docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md, autorun log.
      No host UI cut-over; that lands in a follow-up PR.
    
    Risk
    - Low. New helpers are unused at the call sites today; existing
      components keep their current behaviour. Finder commands enforce a
      documented allow-list + path validation before shelling out.
    
    Docs
    - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md, xai-v1.autorun-20260519.
    
    Tests
